# The Holly and the Ivy, arranged by DeepSeek Flash and SZ. A brushed waltz bass, Rhodes and muted trumpet, and a slow turn at the end.
title: The Holly and the Ivy
composer: Traditional (English)
arranger: DeepSeek Flash & SZ
about: An English folk carol. The holly's white flowers, red berries and prickly leaves stand for the nativity, the drops of blood and the crown of thorns. Cecil Sharp collected the tune from singers in the early 1900s; the words were printed as a broadside by 1823.
year: traditional
source: public-domain
category: carols
key: F major
style: lofi
tempo: 96
time: 3/4

@bars 48-51 tempo=96..80

